ation_es":"El celular is masculine and singular: lo. The order is no + pronoun + verb: no lo tengo.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-lo-llamo"]},{"id":"es-a2-u10-l03-e05","lesson_id":"es-a2-u10-l03","position":5,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Listen and choose what you hear","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"Lo llamo mañana.","options":["Lo llamo mañana.","La llamo mañana.","Lo llamo ahora.","Los llamo mañana."]},"answer":"Lo llamo mañana.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-lo-llamo"]},{"id":"es-a2-u10-l03-e06","lesson_id":"es-a2-u10-l03","position":6,"type":"order_words","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Put the words in order","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["Lo","llamo","esta","noche"],"translation":"I’ll call him tonight."},"answer":"Lo llamo esta noche.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":25,"words":["es-lo-llamo"]},{"id":"es-a2-u10-l03-e07","lesson_id":"es-a2-u10-l03","position":7,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Listen and answer","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"es.stim.a2-u10-compu","setting":"Marta calls her grandson Nico because her computer has a problem.","speakers":[{"name":"Marta","voice":"a"},{"name":"Nico","voice":"b"}],"rate":0.9,"lines":[{"speaker":"Marta","text":"¡Hola, Nico! La computadora no funciona y no puedo leer los mails."},{"speaker":"Nico","text":"Hola, abuela. ¿Qué pasó con la pantalla?"},{"speaker":"Marta","text":"Está negra. Y ayer cambié la contraseña, pero olvidé la nueva."},{"speaker":"Nico","text":"Tranquila, abuela. Esta tarde voy a tu casa y lo vemos."},{"speaker":"Marta","text":"¡Gracias! ¿Llamo a tu mamá?"},{"speaker":"Nico","text":"No, yo la llamo ahora."}]},"question":"What is wrong with Marta’s computer?","options":["It isn’t working and the screen is black","It is very old","It has no apps","Someone stole it"]},"answer":"It isn’t working and the screen is black","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Marta says “La computadora no funciona” (it isn’t working) and the screen “está negra” (is black).","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"es-a2-u10-l03-e08","lesson_id":"es-a2-u10-l03","position":8,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Listen and answer","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"es.stim.a2-u10-compu","setting":"Marta calls her grandson Nico because her computer has a problem.","speakers":[{"name":"Marta","voice":"a"},{"name":"Nico","voice":"b"}],"rate":0.9,"lines":[{"speaker":"Marta","text":"¡Hola, Nico! La computadora no funciona y no puedo leer los mails."},{"speaker":"Nico","text":"Hola, abuela. ¿Qué pasó con la pantalla?"},{"speaker":"Marta","text":"Está negra. Y ayer cambié la contraseña, pero olvidé la nueva."},{"speaker":"Nico","text":"Tranquila, abuela. Esta tarde voy a tu casa y lo vemos."},{"speaker":"Marta","text":"¡Gracias! ¿Llamo a tu mamá?"},{"speaker":"Nico","text":"No, yo la llamo ahora."}]},"question":"Who is Nico going to call?","options":["His mom","His grandmother","His dad","A friend"]},"answer":"His mom","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Marta asks “¿Llamo a tu mamá?” and Nico answers “Yo la llamo ahora”: la means her, his mom.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"es-a2-u10-l03-e09","lesson_id":"es-a2-u10-l03","position":9,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Translate into Spanish","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"My grandmother? I see her on Sundays."},"answer":"¿Mi abuela? La veo los domingos.","accepted_answers":["Mi abuela, la veo los domingos.","¿Mi abuela? La veo todos los domingos."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["es-la-veo"]},{"id":"es-a2-u10-l03-e10","lesson_id":"es-a2-u10-l03","position":10,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Answer in Spanish","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"¿Llamas a tu papá hoy?","translation":"Answer yes, using a pronoun instead of tu papá (e.g. «Sí, lo llamo hoy»)."},"answer":"Sí, lo llamo hoy.","accepted_answers":["Sí, lo llamo.","Sí, hoy lo llamo.","Sí, lo llamo hoy"],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["es-lo-llamo"]},{"id":"es-a2-u10-l04-e01","lesson_id":"es-a2-u10-l04","position":1,"type":"translation_choice","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"What does “le escribo” mean?","payload":{"type":"translation_choice","word":"le escribo","options":["I write to him","I talk to them","I call him","I see her"]},"answer":"I write to him","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":12,"words":["es-le-escribo"]},{"id":"es-a2-u10-l04-e02","lesson_id":"es-a2-u10-l04","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complete the sentence","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"___ escribo un mensaje a mi hermana.","translation":"I’m writing a message to my sister.","options":["Le","Les","La","Lo"]},"answer":"Le","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"My sister receives the message, so she gets le (to her). La would mean that you write her, as if she were the message.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-le-escribo","es-el-mensaje"]},{"id":"es-a2-u10-l04-e03","lesson_id":"es-a2-u10-l04","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complete the sentence","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"___ hablo a los estudiantes en inglés.","translation":"I talk to the students in English.","options":["Les","Le","Los","Lo"]},"answer":"Les","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Los estudiantes are several people who hear you: les (to them). Le is for one person.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-les-hablo"]},{"id":"es-a2-u10-l04-e04","lesson_id":"es-a2-u10-l04","position":4,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Listen and choose what you hear","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"Le escribo a mi papá.","options":["Le escribo a mi papá.","Les escribo a mis papás.","Le escribo a mi mamá.","Le hablo a mi papá."]},"answer":"Le escribo a mi papá.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-le-escribo"]},{"id":"es-a2-u10-l04-e05","lesson_id":"es-a2-u10-l04","position":5,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Complete the sentence","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"¿El mail para Juan? Ya ___ mando.","translation":"The email for Juan? I’ll send it to him right away.","options":["se lo","le lo","lo le","se la"]},"answer":"se lo","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Le + lo becomes se lo; “le lo” does not exist. The person goes first, then the thing: se lo. El mail is masculine, so lo, not la.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["es-se-lo-mando","es-el-mail"]},{"id":"es-a2-u10-l04-e06","lesson_id":"es-a2-u10-l04","position":6,"type":"order_words","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Put the words in order","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["Se","lo","mando","mañana"],"translation":"I’ll send it to him tomorrow."},"answer":"Se lo mando mañana.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":25,"words":["es-se-lo-mando"]},{"id":"es-a2-u10-l04-e07","lesson_id":"es-a2-u10-l04","position":7,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Read and answer","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"es.stim.a2-u10-facultad","document":"message","setting":"A text message from Valentina (Valen) to her dad.","from":"Valen","to":"Papá","lines":["¡Hola, papá!","Te mando el mail de la facultad con el horario de los exámenes. ¿Lo recibiste?","Para leerlo, tienes que bajar la app de la facultad.","La contraseña te la mando por mensaje.","¿No funciona? Llámame esta noche.","Besos, Vale